 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<p>Bottled mentsuyu works instead of the homemade concentrate — dilute it by its label.</p>",
   "title_html": "Short on time"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Just One Cookbook reuses the spent kombu and katsuobushi in homemade furikake (a different mix from the <a href=\"furikake.html\">furikake</a> here).</p>",
   "title_html": "Leftover kombu and bonito"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Grated daikon, sesame seeds or grated ginger in the dipping cup.</li><li>For gluten-free, use 100% buckwheat soba (ju-wari) and tamari instead of soy sauce.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Variations"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Soba clumps and loses its texture as it sits; the sauce is the part to make ahead.</p>",
   "title_html": "Cook just before serving"
  }
 ],
